    {
      "ts": 1791495249.7240179,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "The change excludes superseded execute children from the closable check and requires at least one non-superseded child, as the spec asks. A failed child still blocks closable. Both named tests are defined as unittest methods in DecisionPoints, and the execute_child helper accepts the status and merged_into fields they pass. I did not run the tests, so I haven't confirmed they pass. I only read the planner_runs.py and test_planner_runs.py hunks. Superseded children are still counted in the queued/running check over all children, which is fine because a superseded task is not queued or running.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/planner_runs.py",
            "line": 363,
            "issue": "Direct c[\"status\"] indexing matches the existing ch[\"status\"] usage nearby, so it is consistent. If the all-superseded case matters, it correctly yields no closable point and leaves the goal to the Planner. No test covers that case.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
